#chip 18F24J50, 8
#osc INTOSC

'Change1657 test: fixes ConfigNameMatch picking the wrong config setting on a chip that has
'both a setting literally named OSC and settings merely containing OSC as a substring
'(RTCOSC, DSWDTOSC) - the settings list is in reverse order, so the old loose "contains OSC"
'match could reach RTCOSC/DSWDTOSC before the real OSC setting.
'Expect: compiles; the console OSC: line reads "OSC: INTOSC, 8Mhz (Internal oscillator)".
'Before this fix, the same source compiled the correct CONFIG OSC=INTOSC fuse bits, but
'mis-reported the OSC: line as "OSC: , 8Mhz (...)" - the diagnostic text was blank/wrong
'because the reporting lookup (a separate loop from the one that writes the real fuse bits)
'picked up RTCOSC or DSWDTOSC's value instead of OSC's.

Do
Loop
